    },
    {
      "text": "A contradiction is not a bug a contradiction is a gift.",
      "timestamp_sec": 747,
      "why": "Inverts the usual product instinct to smooth over conflicting retrieval results."
    },
    {
      "text": "We caught it because one person happened to have both documents open at once. Pure luck. Luck is not a control.",
      "timestamp_sec": 823,
      "why": "Concrete anecdote arguing that contradiction detection must be systematized."
    },
    {
      "text": "Your job as a builder isn't resolve the argument. It's to make sure that the argument happens in front of a human instead of quietly along inside box.",
      "timestamp_sec": 823,
      "why": "A direct design directive that many RAG systems violate by default."
    },
    {
      "text": "Model four. Facts and the guesses have to live in separate box. And the fluent AI loves melting them into one smooth sentence.",
      "timestamp_sec": 892,
      "why": "Identifies fluency itself as the mechanism that destroys epistemic labeling."
    },
    {
      "text": "Label your guesses, a tag, a color, anything that survives being copy pasted into someone else's slides three weeks later.",
      "timestamp_sec": 957,
